---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { SITE, RESUME, PROJECTS } from "../config/site";
---

<Layout
  title={`About | ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`${SITE.title} building high-performance mobile and web systems. Background in React Native, backend systems, and open source.`}
>
  <div class="container">
    <article class="about section">
      <a href="/" class="back-link">← Home</a>

      <h1>About</h1>

      <div class="content">
        <p class="intro">
          I'm {SITE.name} — a software engineer who has been writing code
          since 2014. I work across the full stack, from mobile apps to backend
          services to the infrastructure that connects them.
        </p>

        <h2>What I Work On</h2>
        <p>
          Most of my recent work has been in React Native and mobile
          development — building performance-critical features like real-time
          GPS tracking, video streaming, offline-first architectures, and
          systems that need to stay reliable at scale.
        </p>
        <p>
          On the backend, I design APIs, data pipelines, and system
          architectures. I care about how services communicate, how data flows
          through a system, and how everything holds up under real-world
          conditions.
        </p>

        <h2>How I Approach Work</h2>
        <p>
          I plan before I build. Before writing any code, I think through the
          system design — data flow, architecture, edge cases, automation. This
          habit has consistently saved weeks of rework on every project I've led.
        </p>
        <p>
          I work incrementally. One module, one feature, one step at a time.
          Each piece is tested, reviewed, and committed before moving to the
          next. I read every line of every diff, including my own.
        </p>
        <p>
          I care about performance from the start, not as a cleanup task. And I
          keep code structured and minimal — because the next person to work on
          it should be able to understand it quickly.
        </p>

        <h2>On AI</h2>
        <p>
          I've been building software long before AI assistants existed.
          Today, I use AI as a tool — for code reviews, iteration, and
          simple tasks. But the logic, the architecture decisions, and the
          accountability are always mine. I review every line before it
          enters a codebase.
        </p>

        <h2>Open Source</h2>
        <p>
          I maintain <a
            href={PROJECTS.expoVideoCache.github}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">{PROJECTS.expoVideoCache.name}</a
          >, a library for HLS video caching in React Native. It's used in
          production apps handling large-scale video delivery.
        </p>
        <p>
          I contribute to open source because I've benefited from it. A
          well-maintained library saves thousands of hours of duplicated work
          across teams and companies.
        </p>

        <h2>Currently</h2>
        <p>
          I'm focused on improving video caching and delivery performance in
          mobile applications — working on adaptive bitrate strategies,
          intelligent prefetching, and reducing startup latency at scale.
        </p>

        <div class="cta-section">
          <a
            href={RESUME.path}
            class="btn btn-ghost"
            download
          >
            Download resume (PDF)
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <Footer />
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-block: var(--space-12);
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    transition: color var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-h1);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .content {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
  }

  .intro {
    font-size: var(--text-h3);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .content h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .content p {
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .cta-section {
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
</style>
